success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Generate audit schema and trigger migrations

Usage: auditstream init [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (defaults to ./auditstream.toml if present)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_CONFIG=]

      --table <SCHEMA.TABLE>
          Table to audit (`schema.table`), repeatable

      --database-url <URL>
          Postgres connection URL (also reads `DATABASE_URL` as fallback)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_DATABASE_URL]

      --exclude <SCHEMA.TABLE.COLUMN>
          Column to exclude from row images (`schema.table.column`), repeatable

      --migrations <MIGRATIONS>
          Migration format to generate (`prisma`, `drizzle`, or `sql`)

          Possible values:
          - prisma:  Prisma SQL migration directory
          - drizzle: Drizzle SQL migration directory
          - sql:     Plain SQL migration files

      --schema <SCHEMA>
          Audit schema name (defaults to `auditstream`)
          
          [env: AUDITSTREAM_SCHEMA=]

      --out <DIR>
          Output directory for generated migration files (defaults per format)

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (`-v` info, `-vv` debug)

      --dry-run
          Print generated migration SQL to stdout without writing any files or updating config

  -q, --quiet
          Silence warnings and info logs (errors only)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

----- stderr -----
